From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:15:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] core: add the parse operator

parse [kind=simple|regex|relaxed] [flags=imsU] Expr with [*] "const" Col[:type] ... [*]

The pattern is compiled once per operator into a .NET regex (1 s match timeout)
with one named group per capture, anchored at the start of the text unless the
pattern begins with '*'. simple and relaxed match string constants literally;
regex uses them as regex fragments. Captures are lazy (".*?" for strings,
digit/number/bool shapes for typed captures) except a capture that ends the
pattern, which takes the rest of the text. Typed captures: string, int, long,
real, decimal, bool, datetime, timespan, guid, dynamic.

Every input row is kept. A row that does not match, or (simple, regex) whose
capture does not convert to its type, gets empty strings / nulls in the new
columns; relaxed nulls only the capture that failed to convert. Non-string
source expressions are converted to text first (dynamic: the string value or
its JSON).

Not done: parse-where, parse-kv.
